fma_mix lane pairs: a 16-bit pair built by v_fma_mixlo_f16 then v_fma_mixhi_f16 is seeded with a v_mov_b32 0 for the
tied input, but the low-half packet preserves only the high half and the high-half packet overwrites it, so no bit of the
seed is ever observed. After allocation, omit a constant whose sole use is the tied input of a mixlo whose sole use is the
tied input of a mixhi (the node keeps its schedule slot and registers; planners count it as zero instructions). The
schedule-preserving form matters: dropping the seed earlier (an undefined source) reshuffled the schedule and lost.
Bit-identical results; afrag kstore cycles -1.0% on gfx1151 (IQ3_S -1.6%, Q4_K / Q3_K -1.3%, IQ4_XS -0.5%).

